     The reason we cannot prove these true theorems is that the
     proofs require such a long time to calculate that even the
     largest supercomputer grinding away for the lifetime of the
     universe cannot accomplish the proof. They require such a
     large but _finite_ [emphasis mine] computing time that we will
     never know if they are true. Other "true" theorems might
     require an infinite computing time -- these are the theorems
