> Artificial intelligence -- most of what I've seen labelled as ai seems to 
> be expert systems, rather than anything I would consider intelligence.  A 
> bureaucracy is an expert system....

The label AI changes over time; it consistently describes those aspects of
intelligence we don't yet know how to model well enough to do engineering
with.  Thus, expert systems was AI when it was a research area, but arguably
isn't now.  At one time, *compilers* were considered AI (back when they were
called "automatic programming".  So it really depends on how you define AI.
-- 
					Eric S. Raymond <esr@snark.thyrsus.com>

